ce, store model + imputer pipeline and a run log artifact.</idea>\n</solution>\n\n<solution>\n<description>Controlled feature engineering with domain-motivated transforms. Hypothesis: this dataset has heavy tails and sentinel encodings; capped/ratio features and a "ever-delinquent" flag will lift AUC over the raw baseline by 0.002–0.005. Plan: keep the same preprocessing fit-on-train discipline and the same LightGBM hyperparameters as the baseline so the only change is features; compare measured validation ROC-AUC on the identical 30k Id set.</description>\n<idea>Cap RevolvingUtilizationOfUnsecuredLines at 1.0 and flag values >1; add log1p of DebtRatio, MonthlyIncome and RevolvingUtilization where non-negative.</idea>\n<idea>Create delinquency aggregates: total past-due count = 30-59 + 60-89 + 90+; binary flags for any 30-59/60-89/90+ lateness; treat {96,98} as "high lateness" bucket mapped to a distinct high count.</idea>\n<idea>Add MonthlyIncomeImputed flag, income-per-person (MonthlyIncome / (NumberOfDependents+1)), and DebtRatio capped at a train-quantile (e.g. 0.995) bound.</idea>\n<idea>Retrain the identical LightGBM and log AUC delta vs baseline; if AUC drops, keep the baseline and record the failed hypothesis.</idea>\n</solution>\n\n<solution>\n<description>Ensemble/stability path: average LightGBM with a shallow high-bias variant plus a logistic/HistGradientBoosting model on standardized features. Hypothesis: this dataset\'s AUC is mostly bias-limited and a small ensemble reduces variance on the fixed validation set, giving a modest but real gain (~0.001–0.003). Cost: ~2–3× baseline runtime, still CPU-only, ~2GB RAM.</description>\n<idea>Train HistGradientBoostingClassifier (sklearn, seed=42) on median-imputed, quantile-clipped features; log AUC.</idea>\n<idea>Train a LightGBM variant with num_leaves=15, feature_fraction=0.8, more estimators for regularization; log AUC.</idea>\n<idea>Blend by rank-average (0.5/0.3/0.2 weights tuned only on the 120k train via internal split, not on the fixed validation labels more than once) and report the single measured validation AUC.</idea>\n<idea>Persist the chosen winner model + preprocessing and regenerate validation and prediction CSVs from it only.</idea>\n</solution>\n\n<solution>\n<description>Error analysis and calibration check before finalizing. Hypothesis: at very low predicted probability the model may systematically under-separate borderline defaulters; calibration inspection will reveal whether further feature work is warranted or whether we should stop at the best measured AUC. Plan: bucket validation predictions into deciles, compare mean predicted probability vs. observed positive rate (using the private-scored AUC only through the evaluator return, not by reading hidden labels ourselves), and examine false negatives among high-confidence band. Do not ship threshold tuning — the metric needs probabilities.</description>\n<idea>Produce reliability-style decile table on train-side out-of-fold predictions (internal split) since hidden validation labels are unavailable.</idea>\n<idea>Inspect misranked high-risk cases: compare feature distributions of false negatives vs true positives in internal split to spot missing features.</idea>\n<idea>Confirm predictions.csv has exactly 101503 rows in test.csv Id order, finite [0,1] probabilities, no index column; confirm validation CSV has 30000 rows aligned to validation Ids.</idea>\n<idea>Save artifacts: model binary, preprocessing object, measured validation ROC-AUC, and a short inference README; return both file paths.</idea>\n</solution>', role='assistant', tool_calls=None, function_call=None, provider_specific_fields=None), provider_specific_fields={})], usage=Usage(completion_tokens=1212, prompt_tokens=1538, total_tokens=2750, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=PromptTokensDetailsWrapper(audio_tokens=None, cache_write_tokens=None, cached_tokens=0, image_tokens=None, text_tokens=None), prompt_cache_hit_t