et, hyperparameters, seed=42, and the exact pipeline used to generate both files. Return both file paths.</ideas>\n<local_experiments>\n<experiment>\n<id>round-001-experiment-01</id>\n<title>LGBM Baseline + Audit</title>\n<description>**Hypothesis.** A CPU LightGBM binary classifier with domain-aware feature engineering, median imputation, and multi-seed bagging establishes a strong, reproducible ROC-AUC baseline for predicting SeriousDlqin2yrs=1, materially above chance.\n\n**Best measured version.** The highest fixed-split validation score achieved was **0.8705** (from the 33-feature 5-seed bag of the tuned `num_leaves=15, lr=0.03, reg_lambda=1.0, min_child_samples=40, subsample=0.9, colsample_bytree=0.8` config, `n_estimators≈371` chosen by internal early stopping). Note: its internal holdout AUC was 0.86825 — slightly *below* the 3-way rank blend that measured 0.86872 on holdout — yet it scored best on the fixed split, illustrating holdout/fixed-split drift at this tight margin (0.868–0.871 range). The engine-recorded best is 0.8705, so that is reported as champion.\n\n**Processing.**\n- Median imputation of `MonthlyIncome` (5390) and `NumberOfDependents` (0), fit on the 120k training rows only.\n- Sentinel codes 96/98 in the three delinquency columns capped at 20; captured by a `delinq_sentinel` flag.\n- Revolving utilization clipped to [0, 1.5] plus a `ru_gt1_flag`.\n- Engineered features: missing flags, `total_delinq`, `delinq_weighted`, `ru_x_delinq`, `debt_per_income`, `income_per_dependent/line`, `log_MonthlyIncome/DebtRatio`, `debt_per_line`, `has_delinq_any`, `age_x_delinq`, `re_loan_ratio`, `util_x_dti`, `debt_pressure`, `ru_over_lines`, `sev_delinq_rate` (33 total features; Id excluded).\n\n**Validation strategy.** Fixed 30000-row validation never used for fitting or early stopping; internal 15% stratified holdout on the 120k train drives `n_estimators` and config. Seed = 42 global; bag seeds [42,7,123,2024,555]; `n_jobs=4`; CPU only.\n\n**Evidence (executed).**\n- Baseline single LGBM (leaves=31, lr=0.05, 19 raw feats): holdout AUC 0.86674 → fixed 0.8680.\n- FE single model: holdout 0.86683 → fixed 0.8685.\n- LGBM+LR rank blend (19 feats): holdout 0.86688 → fixed 0.8693.\n- Tuned leaves=15/lr=0.03 4-seed bag: holdout 0.86856 → fixed 0.8700.\n- 28-feature 4-seed bag: holdout 0.86840 → fixed 0.8702.\n- 3-way rank blend (19bag+28bag+LR, w≈0.5/0.45/0.05): holdout 0.86872 → fixed 0.8703.\n- **33-feature 5-seed bag: holdout 0.86825 → fixed 0.8705 (best).**\n\n**Changes from parent.** Parent was None (first round); established the initial baseline and iterated through feature engineering, model regularization, LR blending, and bagging.\n\n**Artifacts** (working dir): `predictions.csv` (101503 rows, test Id order, Id,Probability), `validation_predictions.csv` (30000 rows), `artifacts/lgbm_bag33_*.txt` (5 boosters, one per seed), `artifacts/run_meta_bag33.json` (features, medians, n_it, seeds, holdout AUC), `artifacts/run_log.txt` (all rounds).\n\n**Load the saved model:** reconstruct features via the `build()` function using the stored `features` and `medians` from `run_meta_bag33.json`, then for each booster `lgb.Booster(model_file=\'artifacts/lgbm_bag33_<seed>.txt\')` and average `predict()` positive probabilities across the 5 seeds.</description>\n<code># Concise outline of best measured approach (33-feature, 5-seed LightGBM bag)\n1. Read train/test/validation CSV from ../input/data.\n2. build(df): median-impute MonthlyIncome & NumberOfDependents (medians from train);\n   cap delinquency sentinels 96/98 -> 20 with flag; clip utilization to 1.5 with gt1 flag;\n   add 33 engineered features (missing flags, ratios, log, delinq aggregates).\n3. y = SeriousDlqin2yrs; internal split train_test_split(test_size=0.15, stratify, seed=42).\n4. Probe LGBM(leaves=15, lr=0.03, reg_lambda=1.0, min_child_samples=40, subsample=0.9,\n   colsample_bytree=0.8) with early_stopping(100) -> n_it ~371.\n5. Bag 5 seeds [42,7,123,2024,555] on